### Advantages

- Each blcok augments on top of each other 
    - The input is essentially kept and passed through all the layers. The layers know what the input is and makes subsequent processing easier

- Shorter gradient paths
    - There are 2 gradient paths that backprop take: Through and around
    - Lets the earlier gradients stay in its original shape
- Easier to build heavier and deeper models

### Concerns

- Shape mismatch 
    - Need to reshape before adding
- Many many more weights
    - If used in concatenation
    - prefer addiation over concatenation for mahy more blcoks
    - goal: have most blocks use addition w/ matching in/out shapes


